    TITLE  :  Borland Ships Rad Pack for Delphi




                BORLAND SHIPS RAD PACK FOR DELPHI
        New Companion Tool Set for Shorter Development Cycles

       SCOTTS VALLEY, Calif. -- June 19, 1995 -- Borland
  International Inc. has begun shipping RAD Pack for Delphi, a
  companion tool kit that combines many of Borland’s award-winning
  developer productivity products into one competitively-priced
  package. Supporting Delphi and Delphi Client/Server, Borland's
  rapid application development tools for Windows and
  client/server, the Delphi RAD Pack gives developers a collection
  of powerful tools to speed development cycles and increase
  productivity.
       "Since Delphi began shipping in February, it has quickly
  gained industry acceptance as an essential development tool for
  Windows and client/server developers," said Richard Gorman, vice
  president of Borland Product Marketing. "In response to Delphi's
  growing developer community, Borland is offering the Delphi RAD
  Pack as a convenient way to utilize the add-on tools most
  commonly requested by Delphi customers."
       The Delphi RAD Pack includes the Delphi Visual Component
  Library source code, Resource Workshop, Resource Expert, Visual
  Solutions Pack, Delphi Language Reference Guide, and Turbo
  Debugger.

       The following is a description of the tools provided in the
  Delphi RAD Pack:

     *   Delphi Visual Component Library source code -- contains
         source code for over 70 components in Delphi, which
         developers can study and modify to create custom
         components.
     *   Resource Workshop -- allows developers to extract and
         modify standard Windows resources, such as icons, cursors,
         bitmaps, and dialogs.
     *   Resource Expert -- converts standard resource scripts into
         Delphi forms.
     *   Visual Solutions Pack -- a collection of VBX custom
         controls including, spreadsheet control, WYSIWYG word
         processors, asynchronous communications, image editors and
         many eye-catching gadgets.
     *   Delphi Language Reference Guide -- a printed reference of
         the Object Pascal language, including an in-depth







